From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ricardo Pardini <ricardo@pardini.net>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 16:32:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/arm-smmu-qcom: Use identity domain for MSM8998 MDSS

The MDSS on MSM8998 keeps scanning out the bootloader splash framebuffer
when the MMSS SMMU probes. Attaching it to a translated default domain
makes every scanout fetch fault (iova inside the splash region), and the
OnePlus 5 firmware resets into crashdump mode.

Use an identity default domain for qcom,msm8998-mdss like the other
Qualcomm MDSS instances, so the splash survives until the display driver
takes over.
---
 drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
index 60688d834e11..59d2531e283a 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
@@ -411,6 +411,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id qcom_smmu_client_of_match[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,glymur-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,mdp4" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,mdss" },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,msm8998-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,msm8998-mss-pil" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,qcm2290-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sar2130p-mdss" },
-- 
